{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25600146",
      "title": "More Redux Basics",
      "sourceHash": "4d69d2a9b7cb00fc3139543def28d0d3e64392b3e4475754d462dbbe4f281137",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 4.31,
          "en": "We are dispatching an action here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.31,
          "end": 7.33,
          "en": "and that action has a type of increment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.33,
          "end": 9.19,
          "en": "Typically when using Redux,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.19,
          "end": 13.41,
          "en": "the goal is to do different things inside of the reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.41,
          "end": 15.72,
          "en": "for different actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.72,
          "end": 19.6,
          "en": "And that's why you get the action as a second argument here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.6,
          "end": 22.82,
          "en": "You get the current state and then the action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.82,
          "end": 27.28,
          "en": "that was dispatched that caused this reducer to run.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.28,
          "end": 29.6,
          "en": "And therefore in the reducer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.6,
          "end": 32.4,
          "en": "we can of course, look into this action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.4,
          "end": 34.81,
          "en": "We can check if the action.type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.81,
          "end": 37.643,
          "en": "is equal to increment for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.98,
          "end": 42.21,
          "en": "And if that's the case, then let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.21,
          "end": 46.5,
          "en": "I wanna return this increment that counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.5,
          "end": 49.01,
          "en": "Otherwise, if a different action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.01,
          "end": 52.96,
          "en": "like the default initialization action was dispatched,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.96,
          "end": 56.033,
          "en": "I wanna return the unchanged state let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.91,
          "end": 58.76,
          "en": "and then we'll also change the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.76,
          "end": 60.4,
          "en": "we have in our state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.4,
          "end": 62.6,
          "en": "because now for the initialization,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.6,
          "end": 65.13,
          "en": "we will not increment the counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.13,
          "end": 68.263,
          "en": "but return the unchanged default state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.5,
          "end": 71.33,
          "en": "And then for the increment action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.33,
          "end": 73.763,
          "en": "we will return the updated counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.61,
          "end": 76.73,
          "en": "So with this little change made",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.73,
          "end": 80.55,
          "en": "if we execute this file again, we now have counter one here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.55,
          "end": 84.143,
          "en": "because for the initialization, it's no longer incremented.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.05,
          "end": 89.58,
          "en": "And that we can, of course, also dispatch other actions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.58,
          "end": 93.443,
          "en": "we could dispatch an action of type, decrement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.63,
          "end": 97.41,
          "en": "So with an identifier of detriment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.41,
          "end": 100.75999999999999,
          "en": "then we just need to add the appropriate code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.75999999999999,
          "end": 104.32300000000001,
          "en": "If action.type equals decrement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.72,
          "end": 108.93,
          "en": "and then just return our new state object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.93,
          "end": 110.15,
          "en": "where counter is set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.15,
          "end": 114.173,
          "en": "to the state.counter minus one, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.37,
          "end": 118.493,
          "en": "If we do this and save doesn't run our file again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.74000000000001,
          "end": 123.47,
          "en": "we have counter one counter zero as outputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.47,
          "end": 126.6,
          "en": "This first output is coming from our subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 126.6,
          "end": 129.01,
          "en": "after the increment action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.01,
          "end": 131.2,
          "en": "and then we change the state again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 131.2,
          "end": 133.35,
          "en": "hence the subscription triggers again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.35,
          "end": 135.63,
          "en": "and to therefore we now see counter zero",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.63,
          "end": 137.823,
          "en": "because we decrease the counter here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.03,
          "end": 141.7,
          "en": "That's how Redux works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.7,
          "end": 145.03,
          "en": "Now there is a bit more to it and more things you can do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.03,
          "end": 149.89,
          "en": "but that is the heart of Redux and of how it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.89,
          "end": 152.97,
          "en": "Obviously, we're not using it with React here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.97,
          "end": 156.65,
          "en": "but that is how Redux works no matter how you use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.65,
          "end": 161.55,
          "en": "And it indeed isn't a library restricted to React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 161.55,
          "end": 165.55,
          "en": "you can use Redux in any JavaScript project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.55,
          "end": 167.47,
          "en": "There even are implementations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 167.47,
          "end": 170.38,
          "en": "for other programming languages as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.38,
          "end": 174.62,
          "en": "But of course here we are going to use it with React though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.62,
          "end": 176.72,
          "en": "And therefore in the next lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.72,
          "end": 180.03,
          "en": "let's now explore how we would use Redux",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.03,
          "end": 182.123,
          "en": "in a React application.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}